  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Briefly explain the concept of plate tectonics and its role in orogeny.', 'Plate tectonics is the theory that the Earth''s rigid outer shell (lithosphere) is broken into large and small plates that move slowly (a few cm per year) over the weak, partly molten asthenosphere, driven by mantle convection, ridge push and slab pull. Plates interact at three kinds of boundaries: divergent (plates move apart - mid-ocean ridges, rift valleys), convergent (plates move towards each other - subduction zones and collision zones) and transform (plates slide past each other - e.g. San Andreas Fault). Most earthquakes, volcanoes and mountain belts occur along these boundaries.
Role in orogeny (mountain building): mountains form mainly at convergent boundaries. Where oceanic crust subducts under a continent, compression and volcanism build mountains like the Andes; ocean-ocean subduction forms island arcs; and where two continents collide, neither subducts easily, so the crust is folded, thrust faulted, thickened, metamorphosed and uplifted into great ranges - the Himalaya formed by the collision of the Indian Plate with the Eurasian Plate from about 50 million years ago, and are still rising as India keeps moving north.', null, '[{"point": "Plate tectonics: lithosphere broken into rigid plates moving over the asthenosphere (mantle convection, ridge push, slab pull); boundaries - divergent, convergent, transform with associated earthquakes, volcanoes", "marks": 2.5}, {"point": "Role in orogeny: mountains form at convergent boundaries - ocean-continent subduction (Andes), ocean-ocean (island arcs), continent-continent collision (Himalaya: India-Eurasia ~50 Ma) by folding, thrust faulting, crustal thickening, metamorphism, uplift", "marks": 2.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation') and t.slug = 'geology'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-3'), 'standard', 5,
