  values ('ME', 'passage', 'Case I: Preliminary landslide study
Landslides are one of the most significant natural hazards affecting mountainous and hilly terrains globally, affecting the environment, infrastructure and human safety. Bhutan, located in the eastern Himalayas, has rugged topography, fragile geology and heavy precipitation, especially during the monsoon, and faces tremendous challenges from landslides.
Scenario: A major landslide has occurred in the southern part of the country, an area of mixed soil and rock types of the Lesser Himalaya with steep and rugged topography and heavy monsoon rainfall averaging over 4000 mm per year. The landslide has caused significant damage to local infrastructure, including roads and residential areas. As a geologist, you have been assigned to conduct a preliminary study of the landslide and prepare a preliminary report outlining the key findings and recommendations.
Information you may use: describe the site visit methodology and data collected (geological formations, soil properties, slope geometry, hydrological conditions), the extent of the landslide and affected infrastructure, vegetation and landscape changes; characterise the site (rock types, soils, slope angles, structures; rainfall, groundwater, seepage; vegetation and land use); analyse triggering factors (rainfall, seismic activity, slope stability, human activities), failure mechanisms and a qualitative stability assessment; and give preliminary recommendations (stabilisation, drainage, land use changes), immediate actions including further detailed studies, and long-term measures.
Write the following section of your report:

Introduction: overview of the landslide event and objectives of the study. (5 marks)', 'Overview: during the peak of the monsoon, after several days of heavy rainfall, a large landslide occurred on a steep slope in southern Bhutan, in the Lesser Himalayan zone characterised by weathered phyllites, schists and quartzites with thick colluvial soil, and annual rainfall exceeding 4000 mm. The slide (approximately described by its length, width and estimated volume) blocked and damaged a section of the national/feeder road, destroyed or damaged several houses and threatens other homes, farmland and utilities (water supply, power lines). Residents were evacuated as a precaution.
Objectives of the preliminary study: (1) document the extent and characteristics of the landslide and the damage; (2) describe the geological, geomorphological and hydrological conditions of the site; (3) identify the triggering and causative factors and the probable failure mechanism; (4) carry out a qualitative assessment of present slope stability and risk to people and infrastructure; and (5) recommend immediate safety measures, further detailed investigations and long-term mitigation.', null, '[{"point": "Overview: location (southern Bhutan, Lesser Himalaya), date/ timing (monsoon), type and approximate size, damage to roads and houses, people affected", "marks": 2.5}, {"point": "Objectives: document event, identify causes/ triggers and failure mechanism, assess current stability and risk, recommend immediate and long-term measures, identify further studies", "marks": 2.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation') and t.slug = 'geology'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-3'), 'standard', 5,
    540, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
    null, null,
    '{"verdict": "pass", "issues": [], "checker_notes": "Model answer, marking guide and rubric written by Claude from the RCSC paper; facts were checked against what is widely published, but please read before publishing. Real past-paper questions keep RCSC wording.", "batch": "ME Paper III (Technical, Geology): BCSE 2024, batch 1", "source": {"title": "BCSE 2024 Main Examination, Technical Paper III, Geology", "year": 2024, "url": "https://rcsc.gov.bt/technical-paper-iii/"}}'::jsonb, 'me-technical-3-geo2024-case1', 1, null, null, (select id from public.specialisations where code = 'geology'), null)
  returning id
)
