Limitations: state some of the major limitations of the study and propose key means to address these constraints. (5 marks)', 'Limitations: much of Bhutan has only regional-scale geological maps, and remote high-altitude areas are poorly studied because of rugged terrain, snow, dense forest and difficult access; there is little subsurface, geochemical, geophysical and drilling data, so resource estimates are uncertain; the ages and activity of faults and the history of past large earthquakes are not well known; the national seismic and GPS networks are still limited; and some exploration data are old, unpublished or confidential.
Means to address them: systematic large-scale geological mapping supported by remote sensing (satellite imagery, LiDAR, drones); regional geochemical and geophysical (magnetic, gravity) surveys followed by drilling of promising targets; geochronology and palaeo-seismology studies; expansion of seismic and GPS monitoring networks; collaboration with international universities and geological surveys; training of national geologists; and a national geoscience database with open access to data.', null, '[{"point": "Limitations: limited detailed geological mapping (large-scale maps, remote/ inaccessible areas), little subsurface/ geochemical/ geophysical data, uncertain ages and fault activity, limited seismic network/ GPS stations, confidential or old exploration data", "marks": 3}, {"point": "Address: systematic large-scale mapping, remote sensing/ LiDAR, geochemical and geophysical surveys, drilling, geochronology, denser seismic/ GPS networks, collaboration with international institutions, capacity building, open data", "marks": 2}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
